      "writtenOn": "2025-06-24T10:47:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree, if pkvm is compromised, there is a risk of attacker to reprivilege the host. But if pkvm is compromised, then all bets are already off isn\u0027t it? I also agree with not continuing the boot, but tainting the kernel and booting with p partially deprivileged cpus doesn\u0027t appeal to me much. I could also go a bit further to zero out the reprivilege code once the pkvm has been fully initialized so that attacker would not be able to use the logic any more if pkvm is compromised. What do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "405ab7f5_adc313d5",
      "revId": "948704b1f794fbc32de454613cdcd2ae4bf3b2b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
